M06 non-key conversation callbacks lost to a key-conversation preemption.
ActiveConversationClass::Start_Conversation stops a non-key conversation
with INTERRUPTED at once while a key conversation (M06_CON001/059/060)
plays. Retail called Monitor_Conversation after Start_Conversation, so that
stop reached no script and the gated effect was lost:
- M06_GDI_Prisoner: prisoner stays stationary, hidden objective 607 lost;
- M06_Activate_Secret_Door: already_poked stays set, the stash bookcase
  never opens and hidden objective 608 is lost;
- M06_Civ_Prisoner: conversation stays true, hidden objective 605 lost;
- M06_Resistance_Raider_DLS: no grenade launcher, raider never pokable;
- M06_Assistance_Farmer_DLS: no grenade launcher, maintenance-shaft
  conversation trigger to 101357 never sent;
- M06_KaneHead: the hologram head is never removed.

Register the monitor before Start_Conversation (poke state set first) so
the immediate stop reaches Action_Complete synchronously. Poke scripts
re-arm the poke on an INTERRUPTED end (GDI prisoner, secret door, raider;
the civilian prisoner already cleared `conversation` on INTERRUPTED; it now
re-shows its poke indicator and skips its health drop until a talk really
starts). The farmer runs its
ENDED branch once for an INTERRUPTED raised inside Start_Conversation only
(transient, unsaved flag). KaneHead already treated INTERRUPTED like ENDED.
Without a key conversation Start_Conversation never touches the monitor
array, so the ENDED path, its timing and every effect are unchanged.

Cosmetic: M06_Objective_Controller marks 609 and 603 accomplished when they
are added after their completion custom already arrived (alarm terminal
before M06_CON060; Sydney relocated before the war-room hack). 603 uses a
new saved flag on unused id 3; older saves load it as false.

